# Copy to voice-pipes/.env — the launcher (launch-stack.ps1 / launch-stack.sh)
# loads it and passes the keys through to the containers BY NAME, so values
# never appear in the compose file or `docker inspect`. Values already set in
# your shell take precedence. The config wizard writes this file automatically
# when you enter keys interactively.
#
# NONE of these are required for the local-only stack (local STT/LLM/TTS).
# Set only what your chosen providers need.

# OpenAI — Realtime S2S provider, OpenAI TTS, or any OpenAI-compatible LLM
#OPENAI_API_KEY=

# Google — GEMINI_API_KEY is for the Gemini Live realtime provider;
# GOOGLE_API_KEY is for Gemini TTS (they are read separately).
#GEMINI_API_KEY=
#GOOGLE_API_KEY=

# ElevenLabs — API key for TTS / Agents; agent id for the Agents S2S worker
# (used when the config sets agent_id_env instead of a literal agent_id).
#ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=
#ELEVENLABS_AGENT_ID=

# AssemblyAI — streaming STT provider
#ASSEMBLYAI_API_KEY=

# Google Cloud STT (Chirp 3) — no API key: it uses Application Default
# Credentials. GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT names the project when the credential
# doesn't; GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS is a service-account key path as
# seen INSIDE the worker container (mount it, e.g. under models/).
#GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT=
#GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS=

# Hugging Face — only needed to download gated models (e.g. Gemma)
#HF_TOKEN=

# Three credentials, three trust domains. The shipped configs refuse to start
# without the client and internal tokens; launch-stack generates all three
# into this file. Each gates one surface:
#   VP_CLIENT_TOKEN   end-user WebSocket transport (/ws) on every worker
#   VP_ADMIN_TOKEN    the orchestrator's admin API and host extensions
#   VP_INTERNAL_TOKEN machine-to-machine: worker registration, heartbeats,
#                     events, and the worker debug API
# Setting a token turns enforcement on for its surface; an empty value counts
# as unset. The shipped deploy configs set `required = true`, so a missing
# token is a startup failure there rather than an open surface; a config
# without it runs open and warns when it binds a non-loopback address.
#VP_CLIENT_TOKEN=
#VP_ADMIN_TOKEN=
#VP_INTERNAL_TOKEN=
